Extend the plugin-registry layout fix from vcpkg PR #53664 to monolithic builds:
https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/pull/53664

Patch 009 moves Windows SHARED component resources to bin/usd. Monolithic
components are OBJECT libraries, so their resources remain in lib/usd. Keep
the root registry beside those resources so its relative Includes resolve.
This preserves Falcor2's existing monolithic package layout; Falcor2 stages
the complete resource tree beside its runtime and sets the plugin search path.

diff --git a/cmake/macros/Public.cmake b/cmake/macros/Public.cmake
--- a/cmake/macros/Public.cmake
+++ b/cmake/macros/Public.cmake
@@ -1072,10 +1072,12 @@ function(pxr_setup_plugins)
     # Plug anchors its default search path to the directory holding the plug
     # library and looks for "<that directory>/usd/plugInfo.json".  The top
     # level registry must therefore be installed next to the per-library
-    # resource trees, which _pxr_library places under the same directory the
-    # shared libraries themselves are installed to.
-    if(WIN32)
+    # resource trees. The vcpkg layout patch moves SHARED component resources
+    # to bin/usd on Windows, but monolithic OBJECT components keep lib/usd.
+    # Extend https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/pull/53664 to keep the registry
+    # beside those resources in both build modes.
+    if(WIN32 AND NOT PXR_BUILD_MONOLITHIC)
         _get_install_dir("${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}/usd" pluginRegistryDir)
     else()
         _get_install_dir("${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/usd" pluginRegistryDir)
     endif()
